  <!--
    English (base) UI strings for TransPeek Windows.
    - Code reads these through TransPeek.Services.AppStrings.Get(key, fallback):
      the fallback is the same English text, so the UI stays English even if
      a lookup fails (e.g. a missing .pri in an unpackaged build).
    - XAML reads these through x:Uid on the element (resw name = Uid.Property);
      the English literal stays in the XAML as the fallback.
    - Adding a language later = adding Strings/<bcp47>/Resources.resw with the
      same keys. No code or XAML change. Roadmap (Manh, 2026-11-11):
      vi (Vietnamese) first, then zh-Hans (Chinese Simplified), then ko (Korean).
    - NOT in here: Core strings (TransPeek.Core stays English-only literals —
      UpdateChecker, DictionaryLink.ValidationError, Tesseract Status), language
      endonyms ("Tiếng Việt", "中文 (简体)", "한국어", … — a language is always
      shown in its own name), and developer comments.
  -->
